@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@
+# Supply-chain policy
+
+This document records how dependency trust is enforced for Snowride. It exists
+because the 2026-10-03 audit found two provisional gaps:
+
+- **SUPPLY-P2-001** — license and vulnerability enforcement was host-only (the
+  daily `scripts/assurance/assurance.sh` lane), not merge-gating.
+- **SUPPLY-P2-002** — install (lifecycle) scripts were allowlisted for several
+  dependencies without documented provenance checks.
+
+## Merge-gating checks
+
+[`.github/workflows/supply-chain.yml`](../.github/workflows/supply-chain.yml)
+runs on every pull request that touches `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, or
+`scripts/license-assurance.mjs`:
+
+| Gate | Command | Scope | Failure |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| License allow-list | `node scripts/license-assurance.mjs` | production dependency tree | blocking |
+| Production advisories | `npm audit --omit=dev --audit-level=high` | production dependencies | advisory (see note) |
+| Registry signatures | `npm audit signatures` | packages installed by `npm ci` | advisory (see note) |
+
+The production advisory check runs advisory rather than blocking because the
+current production tree carries one high advisory in the transitive runtime
+dependency `@grpc/grpc-js`; making it fatal would red every pull request until
+that dependency is bumped (tracked as a PR open question). `npm audit
+signatures` is likewise advisory because the registry returns no public key for
+`@playwright/test@1.63.0`'s attestation (EMISSINGSIGNATUREKEY). The license
+allow-list — the half of SUPPLY-P2-001 that was previously missing entirely
+from merge time — is fully blocking. Once the two advisories clear, both checks
+should be promoted to blocking.
+
+These duplicate the intent of the daily host lane so a disallowed license or a
+high-severity advisory cannot enter `main` between scheduled runs. The daily
+lane in `scripts/assurance/assurance.sh` remains the scheduled recurrence and
+ledger record.
+
+## Install-script allowlist
+
+The root `package.json` carries an `allowScripts` inventory of the packages
+whose `postinstall`/install lifecycle scripts are knowingly accepted during
+`npm ci` (npm runs lifecycle scripts by default; `npm ci --ignore-scripts`
+disables all of them). Each entry is reviewed on the cadence below.
+
+| Package | Why its install script is required |
+|---|---|
+| `esbuild@0.28.2`, `esbuild@0.25.12` | Installs/validates the platform-native esbuild binary used by the bundler and vitest. The binary is pinned through the lockfile and registry signatures. |
+| `protobufjs@7.6.6` | Post-install step for the generated static code used by the realtime transport. Pulled transitively; exact version pinned in the lockfile. |
+| `puppeteer@25.10.0` | Downloads the pinned Chromium build used by the e2e/a11y/perf lanes. Browser revision is fixed by the Puppeteer version, not fetched ad hoc at test time. |
+| `unrs-resolver` | Native resolver binding used by the lint/import toolchain; its post-install link step is required for the package to load. |
+
+Rules:
+
+1. **No new entry without review.** Adding a package to `allowScripts`, or
+   accepting a lockfile change that introduces a new lifecycle-script package,
+   requires an explicit reviewer decision recorded in the PR.
+2. **Provenance first.** `npm audit signatures` must pass in
+   `.github/workflows/supply-chain.yml` before the allowlist is considered
+   current; a package whose registry signature cannot be verified is not
+   accepted.
+3. **Prefer removal.** If an install script can be dropped (for example by
+   using a prebuilt artifact or `--ignore-scripts` plus an explicit build step),
+   do so rather than adding an allowlist entry.
+
+## Verification (manual / release review)
+
+```sh
+npm ci
+node scripts/license-assurance.mjs   # exit 0 = all production licenses allowed
+npm audit --omit=dev --audit-level=high
+npm audit signatures                 # provenance; currently EMISSINGSIGNATUREKEY for @playwright/test
+```
+
+## Related documents
+
+- `scripts/assurance/assurance.sh` — daily OSV/audit/license lane.
+- `scripts/license-assurance.mjs` — offline license allow-list gate.
+- `SECURITY.md` — vulnerability reporting and hardening baseline.
+- SBOM generation/retention is covered by the SBOM step in
+  `.github/workflows/ci-foundation.yml` (SUPPLY-P1-001).
